{
  "id": "queue-keep-going-target",
  "title": "Keep going serves one batch up to keep_going_new_target, then the stop screen returns; an unfinished batch is not owed (ADR-052)",
  "covers": [
    "queue.keep_going_target",
    "queue.keep_going_batch_not_owed"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "Seven kana-only new words (no kanji notes are minted), reviews unlimited, new goal 2. Every answer is Easy, so each card graduates at once and no learning card is ever on a timer.",
    "Steps 0-3: the goal's two cards, then goal_reached with keep_going_available true.",
    "Step 4: the press. The client sends target = new.today + max(1, goal) = 4: exactly two new cards are drawn although five remain and limit is 10; until_stop_parts.new is 2 (left to the target, not the batch).",
    "Steps 5-6: after one of them is answered one is left in sight (until_stop 1).",
    "Step 7 (ADR-052 b, exit mid-batch): the same instant without keep_going: goal_reached, no item, until_stop_parts.new 0. The fourth card of the batch is not owed to Home or the header.",
    "Step 8: back in Review, a fresh press: target = 3 + 2 = 5: a full batch of two again (cards 4 and 5), not the one card left of the old batch.",
    "Steps 9-11: both answered: with the same target the answer is goal_reached with keep_going true and keep_going_available true (two new cards remain). Before C-31 this request served the next new card.",
    "Step 12: a target below new.today (already exceeded, e.g. another device studied): no new card, the same stop screen.",
    "Step 13: keep_going_new_target without keep_going=true is ignored: a normal request.",
    "Step 14: keep_going=true without a target is the endless stream of C-26, unchanged: the two remaining cards.",
    "Steps 15-16: a target that is not a non-negative integer is 422 at /keep_going_new_target.",
    "Steps 17-21: target 7, the last two cards answered: nothing is left anywhere, so the phase is empty with keep_going_available false, with and without keep going (ADR-051 a).",
    "Whole /loop objects are pinned; they are hand-evaluated from contracts/core ReviewLoop (rule 6 Target, examples W3, X1, X2)."
  ],
